==Problem 14== 
Three <imath>\text{A's}</imath>, three <imath>\text{B's}</imath>, and three  <imath>\text{C's}</imath> are placed in the nine spaces so that each row and column contain one of each letter. If <imath>\text{A}</imath> is placed in the upper left corner, how many arrangements are possible?
<asy>
size((80));
draw((0,0)--(9,0)--(9,9)--(0,9)--(0,0));
draw((3,0)--(3,9));
draw((6,0)--(6,9));
draw((0,3)--(9,3));
draw((0,6)--(9,6));
label("A", (1.5,7.5));
</asy>
<imath> \textbf{(A)}\ 2\qquad\textbf{(B)}\ 3\qquad\textbf{(C)}\ 4\qquad\textbf{(D)}\ 5\qquad\textbf{(E)}\ 6 </imath>

[[2008 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14|Solution]]


== Solution ==
There are <imath>2</imath> ways to place the remaining <imath>\text{As}</imath>, <imath>2</imath> ways to place the remaining <imath>\text{Bs}</imath>, and <imath>1</imath> way to place the remaining <imath>\text{Cs}</imath> for a total of <imath>(2)(2)(1) = \boxed{\textbf{(C)}\ 4}</imath>.

